  "details": "VRChat should have a way to reply to declined invitation requests in a visually easy-to read way. Right now you can send a message when you decline a request from someone, but that person cannot respond back.\n\nCurrently the only way to \"reply\" back to a declined invite is by sending another invitation request, but you'll have to click on this invitation to even read the message, it's misleading as it comes across as someone being impatient to join since the message just doesn't show unless you open the request pop-up.\n\n**The idea is simple**;\n\nHave a pop-up with (a brief description of) an (invitation) response that has a reply and dismiss button right next to it.(If it's a brief/shortened version it could include a button to \"foldout\" the message as well.)\n\nUse-cases for this would be instances where someone doesn't want to be joined, for example; when someone's testing something or they're in a private setting but you have a question for them that might be important. You might try to join them to talk to them in person, but if that is off the table it could be useful to leave a simple message instead.\n\nThe argument could be made as to why not leave a message on another platform, but there are multiple arguments to make against that as well.- We have ways to communicate on VRChat and VRChat is a social platform. as a user I'd prefer not to juggle with overlays while in the VR space. Besides that there are plenty of people who do not have other people's socials or want to share their socials with others outside of VRChat.\n\nThese are just a few arguments but I'm sure there are more.\n\nThe goal is not to create a full-fledged chatting system in VRChat, but to create an effective but simple response system that makes sense.\n\n# TLDR:\n\n- **Pop-up for (invitation) replies**:\n\n- (brief) message\n\n- Respond button\n\n- Dismiss button\n\n- Foldout button if message is brief\n\nLove to hear your thoughts.",
